      "obligation": "refuter:10:1",
      "id": "lem-quotient-blocks-preserve-connectedness-and-anticonnectedness",
      "location": "[L1]",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "[L1] says that one quotient block's member blocks can be listed as $A_1,\\dots,A_t$ with every consecutive pair mixed. The cited definitions only give that the member blocks form one mixed-block reachability class, i.e. any two are joined by some mixed chain. They do not imply a single ordering of all members with consecutive mixed pairs. Counterexample: take four original blocks $A,B,C,D$ with mixed pairs exactly $(A,B)$, $(B,C)$, and $(B,D)$, and all other pairs anticomplete. Then all four blocks lie in one $\\mathcal M$-class, hence one quotient block, but no ordering of $A,B,C,D$ has every consecutive pair mixed; such an ordering would be a Hamiltonian path in the star $K_{1,3}$, which does not exist. So [L1] states a stronger and false combinatorial property, and the proof steps built on it are not licensed.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "8c1bda4db7a128cf2a230e8b77052ea7b4a8ccf5a75b10282934ad5b2c99ef0f"
    },
    {
